WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.500
Here's Al-Duha. It opens with an oath: by the morning
brightness, and by the night when it grows still.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:24.987
We select the first three ayat, ending with “your Lord has not forsaken you,
nor does He hate you,” and ask what happened that this needed to be said.

00:00:24.987 --> 00:00:34.687
What happened, it says: revelation paused, and opponents
mocked the Prophet ﷺ, saying his Lord had forsaken him.

00:00:34.687 --> 00:00:41.887
Then Allah's answer in 93:3 denies both things
they suggested: abandonment, and loss of love.

00:00:41.887 --> 00:00:49.487
It also weighs other reports al-Wahidi records,
noting where Ibn Kathir questions one.
